Article 44

(1) Civil Servant Investigators within the Regional Government are given special authority to conduct investigations of criminal acts as referred to in the applicable Criminal Procedure Code.

(2) The authority of the investigator as referred to in paragraph (1) is: a. receiving, seeking, collecting and examining information or reports concerning criminal acts;

b. examining, seeking and collecting information or reports concerning criminal acts;

c. requesting information and evidence from individuals or entities in connection with criminal acts;

d. examining books, records and other documents concerning criminal acts;

e. conducting searches to obtain evidence of bookkeeping, records and other documents and conducting seizures of such evidence;

f. requesting the assistance of experts in the context of carrying out the duties of investigating criminal acts;

g. ordering to stop, prohibiting a person from leaving a room or place when an examination is in progress and examining the identity of the person and or documents carried as referred to in letter e; h. photographing a person related to a criminal act;

i. summoning a person to be heard for information and examined as a suspect or witness;

j. terminating the investigation;

k. taking other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts according to applicable law and which can be accounted for. (3) The investigator as referred to in paragraph (1), shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of the investigation to the public prosecutor through the Investigator of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the applicable Criminal Procedure Code.

